---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { href } from '../../lib/href';
import Widget from '../../components/StiffnessBandwidth.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Dynamic Stiffness, Bandwidth and the Bode Plot — ECE/ME 732">
  <p class="crumb"><a href={href("/interactives/")}>← Interactives</a></p>
  <h1>Dynamic Stiffness, Bandwidth and the Bode Plot</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    The same shaft and the same three state feedback gains, but here the gains
    are the sliders and the bandwidths are what comes out. Each crossing on
    the stiffness plot is set by two gains. Beside it, the same frequencies on
    Bode plots: the velocity loop alone, the position loop's open-loop gain,
    and the closed loop with and without the velocity command. Below, a load
    step and a sine command, solved exactly, so a number read off the Bode plot
    can be checked against the time trace.
  </p>
  <Widget />
</BaseLayout>
